fields.evidenceCards/0/content:
Four weeks, 1.04 million visitors in each group.

Primary metric — purchases per visitor: +0.4% (interval from −1.1% to +1.9%). Statistically insignificant.

Secondary metrics:
— product views per session: +6.2% (+4.8% to +7.6%), significant;
— saves per visitor: +3.1% (+1.4% to +4.8%), significant;
— home screen load time: −180 ms, significant;
— sessions per visitor: +0.2% (−0.9% to +1.3%), insignificant;
— messages to seller per visitor: −5.4% (−7.1% to −3.7%), statistically significant decrease.

Minimum detectable effect (MDE) for the primary metric set before launch: 2%.

fields.evidenceCards/2/content:
The analyst broke down the results by segment after seeing the flat overall result.

Purchases per visitor by recency:
— new visitors (first session): +4.1% (+1.2% to +7.0%);
— returning, under 3 months: +0.9% (−1.8% to +3.6%);
— returning, over 3 months: −1.6% (−3.4% to +0.2%).

His verbatim comment: 'This was not a pre-specified breakdown, and I checked six of them. Treat one significant result out of six as a question, not an answer.'
